{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia","id":965930,"title":"Vampires and Gaia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-08T16:51:55-07:00","id":965930,"title":"Vampires and Gaia","content":"So it just occurred to me that one of the ante vamps called ennoi(or something, the gangrel one) is currently fused with the earth itself. Considering the effect vampires have on spirits, what effect could this be having on gaia herself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T17:42:08-07:00","id":965948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia#post965930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it just occurred to me that one of the ante vamps called ennoi(or something, the gangrel one) is currently fused with the earth itself. Considering the effect vampires have on spirits, what effect could this be having on gaia herself?</div> </div> </div> </div>First things first, that is only the case in the Gehenna book and then only is one of these scenarios. It certainly isn't canon in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> That being said, if this were a thing I would just say (Gangrel) ceases to be. No coming back later, no grand story. It just ceases to exist, having merged with Gaia. Perhaps she forgave it allowing (Gangrel) some sort of peaceful end. <br /> <br /> Gaia continues to be and nothing changes. Ante's aren't anywhere near powerful enough to affect Gaia on any meaningful level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T17:48:32-07:00","id":965952,"title":"","content":"another crossover question?<br /> <br /> How do Demons, or the Imbued fit into the Garou cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:03:58-07:00","id":965956,"title":"","content":"Garou cosmology leaves a lot of room for unknowns. Forgetting their names but the marine mind worms and the underground 6 fingered no eyed monsters are examples. <br /> <br /> Are you asking this question from an in character (Garou) point of view or an OOC viewpoint?<br /> <br /> In character:<br /> I would say Demons are just a form of High Umbral spirit fomori/Possessed.<br /> Hunter's are just motivated humans with fairly minor magical tricks. Hunter came out early enough that there should actually be write-ups for them in there Werewolf books. I know the later breed books address them. The Nagah in particular have something to say about Gaia possibly replacing them (the Nagah).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:25:45-07:00","id":965965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=965956#post965956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou cosmology leaves a lot of room for unknowns. Forgetting their names but the marine mind worms</div> </div> </div> </div>The mind worms are qyrlings, and quite familiar to the Rokea, at least. There's also the Chulorviah, evil cephalopods which incorporate both something like a cross between Leviathan and the Shadow Over Innsmouth, as well as Heinlein's Puppet Masters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the underground 6 fingered no eyed monsters are examples. </div> </div> </div>Vhujunka, though they're still more familiar, at least in presentation, than a lot of things from other games..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you asking this question from an in character (Garou) point of view or an OOC viewpoint?<br /> <br /> In character:<br /> I would say Demons are just a form of High Umbral spirit fomori/Possessed.<br /> Hunter's are just motivated humans with fairly minor magical tricks. Hunter came out early enough that there should actually be write-ups for them in there Werewolf books. I know the later breed books address them. The Nagah in particular have something to say about Gaia possibly replacing them (the Nagah). </div> </div> </div>The Nagah specifically lamented that if one of them were to crop up when they were at work, it would probably be a sign that the Nagah done goofed in an even bigger way than before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:46:17-07:00","id":965977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=965965#post965965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The mind worms are qyrlings, and quite familiar to the Rokea, at least. There's also the Chulorviah, evil cephalopods which incorporate both something like a cross between Leviathan and the Shadow Over Innsmouth, as well as Heinlein's Puppet Masters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Vhujunka, though they're still more familiar, at least in presentation, than a lot of things from other games..</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I'm away from my books and posting from my phone and couldn't remember any of the creature names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T20:00:07-07:00","id":966006,"title":"","content":"Esoteric threats never really come up in my games. I generally find enough to occupy my characters with mortal Fomori and mortal Infernalists. It has gotten to the point where they duck for cover whenever I introduce an adolescent girl because they know that there will be trouble, one way or another, relating to her existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T18:07:55-07:00","id":966507,"title":"","content":"If Gangrel actually did truly fuse with Gaia, then it sounds like Ennoia found a way to transcend the Curse and be forgiven for the Curse of Caine. There is certainly a place in Gaia' for a big blood thirsty Beasty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:46:40-07:00","id":966639,"title":"","content":"No, it just means that Gaia is more powerful than the God that cursed Caine, so She can lift the Curse if she feels it is appropriate. Perhaps Ennoia was transformed into the Celestine of the crust of the Earth by Gaia when She adopted Ennoia. I imagine that Ennoia could be a devestation weapon against the Weaver or Wyrm, if push came to shove. A relevant question though would be could Ennoia then forgive the Curse of the Gangrel and transform them into new Tribes of Changing Breeds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T01:48:09-07:00","id":966677,"title":"","content":"Mmmh, so a Vampire who uses viccissitude 9( earth vast Heaven) or does the same with Animalism 9 (eyes of the forest) has been forgiven by Gaia too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-10-2016, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T03:42:43-07:00","id":966687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=966677#post966677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmh, so a Vampire who uses viccissitude 9( earth vast Heaven) or does the same with Animalism 9 (eyes of the forest) has been forgiven by Gaia too?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No those are just puny Methuselah powers so its just an infection. And I don't think Ennoia would be a Celestine... that is a big jump of power...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T04:31:04-07:00","id":966703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=966677#post966677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmh, so a Vampire who uses viccissitude 9( earth vast Heaven) or does the same with Animalism 9 (eyes of the forest) has been forgiven by Gaia too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all, as they have not transcended the Curse. At best, they are temporary irritants, which are expelled in due time. Ennoia probably had to be merged with the Earth for a thousand years before Gaia decided that she was worth examining. I would suggest, however, that a vampire who had merged with the Earth for a thousand years may be forgiven and, depending on their power, may have been transformed into a spirit.<br /> <br /> You are probably right about a Celestine, an Incarna/Totem would probably be more appropriate. If you generalized the rules, a Methuselah could use similar methods to become a Jaggling while a higher generation vampire could only become a Gaffling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T05:11:27-07:00","id":966717,"title":"","content":"In an End of Times scenario I was creating, the already-weakened Gaia is in the end killed when Ennoia meld with the Earth. While the new &quot;thing-planet&quot; is indeed more strong than the old-Gaia, at the same time is not the spiritual goddess she was. In the end, the Garou (and a great deal of others splats) will find a way to blend the &quot;thing-planet&quot; with what remains of an avatar of the old-Gaia, thus transmuting it in a new young Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T07:43:27-07:00","id":966751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=966717#post966717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In an End of Times scenario I was creating, the already-weakened Gaia is in the end killed when Ennoia meld with the Earth. While the new &quot;thing-planet&quot; is indeed more strong than the old-Gaia, at the same time is not the spiritual goddess she was. In the end, the Garou (and a great deal of others splats) will find a way to blend the &quot;thing-planet&quot; with what remains of an avatar of the old-Gaia, thus transmuting it in a new young Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like it could be an interesting Chronicle, even if I completely disagree with the premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T09:08:34-07:00","id":966780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=966751#post966751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like it could be an interesting Chronicle, even if I completely disagree with the premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The premise that Gaia is already weakened?<br /> As &quot;Gaia is dying&quot; is continually repeated in almost all the WTA books (with Pentex and BSD that take it as their mission), I took it to the further step. When the physical rappresentation of the planet is mystically killed by the giant vampiric parasyte, as with the other earthly rappresentations, this reverberates on the Umbral facet, actually destroying the weakened goddess herself.<br /> <br /> It was a high-crossover chronicle and in the end I will never play it -_-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 09-10-2016, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T09:14:47-07:00","id":966784,"title":"","content":"I don't think that Ennoia merging with Gaia meshes very well with either Werewolf or Vampire mythology or cosmology. I had always just assumed that she melded with the earth physically, not any kind of spiritual union with the earth or Gaia. I think that Gehenna makes more sense when you toss out Werewolf cosmology, just like a lot of things make sense in W:tA when you toss out Vampire cosmology.<br /> <br /> Though, that is just my interpretation, your mileage may very.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 09-10-2016, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T09:15:02-07:00","id":966785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=966780#post966780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The premise that Gaia is already weakened?<br /> As &amp;quot;Gaia is dying&amp;quot; is continually repeated in almost all the WTA books (with Pentex and BSD that take it as their mission), I took it to the further step. When the physical rappresentation of the planet is mystically killed by the giant vampiric parasyte, as with the other earthly rappresentations, this reverberates on the Umbral facet, actually destroying the weakened goddess herself.<br /> <br /> It was a high-crossover chronicle and in the end I will never play it -_-</div> </div> </div> </div>The premise that an Ante could do anything to affect even a weakened Gaia. Supernals can't seem to do it and they are leagues above any Vampire (even Caine).<br /> <br /> Like I said though, it sounds like an interesting Chronicle premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:06:25-07:00","id":966804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=966785#post966785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The premise that an Ante could do anything to affect even a weakened Gaia. Supernals can't seem to do it and they are leagues above any Vampire (even Caine).</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> I actually based this idea on the non-canon scenario of The Last Battleground (Apocalypse book) and figured that while Ennoia alone couldn't certainly kill Gaia (note: Ennoia don't even know what Gaia is, she is only trying to ascend from the vampiric status), but if the Wyrmish forces are so firmly set in destroying her, the Antediluvian would probably be the coin able to tip the scale, taking over in the process the &quot;physical&quot; representation of the planet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=966785#post966785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said though, it sounds like an interesting Chronicle premise.</div> </div> </div> </div> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The complete scenario had strong ties with Werewolf, Vampire, Mage and Wraith. The fact that we stopped playing and that I cannot use it, is still eating at me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:25:51-07:00","id":966815,"title":"","content":"I think that 'Gaia is dying' is a mammalian and avian Changing Breed fallacy. The Ananasi, Mokole, and Rokea seem to just see it more as 'Gaia is changing'. They have survived extinction events before, they will survive another one, even if all of the mammals and birds go extinct in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:41:51-07:00","id":967015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=966815#post966815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that 'Gaia is dying' is a mammalian and avian Changing Breed fallacy. The Ananasi, Mokole, and Rokea seem to just see it more as 'Gaia is changing'. They have survived extinction events before, they will survive another one, even if all of the mammals and birds go extinct in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a writing thing. Some breeds have a fire under their ass. Others have different callings and have to take a longer view. Even the longer-viewed, though, do note that it's very important to do as much as possible as soon as possible to determine what the shape of the new world is going to be, rather than leaving it up to their enemies or some unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:05:02-07:00","id":967056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=966785#post966785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The premise that an Ante could do anything to affect even a weakened Gaia. Supernals can't seem to do it and they are leagues above any Vampire (even Caine).<br /> <br /> Like I said though, it sounds like an interesting Chronicle premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, why couldn't a it? If you were to set off enough nukes and destroy the moon, luna would die and wouldn't be able to do sh*t about it. That's kind of the weakness of both celestines and supernals, they're stuck in a prison inside of which they are Gods, but can't influence anything outside their prison directly. Even Incarna are stuck in the spirit world unable to effect the physical one.<br /> <br /> If ennoia started eating physical earth from the inside, gaia would slowly die with the planet and be unable to do anything beyond beg the changing breads for help. Like how the entire fight with the other supernals has been going for millennia, no of them can directly touch each other or earth and they need minions to do it for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T22:05:16-07:00","id":967169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=967056#post967056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um, why couldn't a it? If you were to set off enough nukes and destroy the moon, luna would die and wouldn't be able to do sh*t about it. That's kind of the weakness of both celestines and supernals, they're stuck in a prison inside of which they are Gods, but can't influence anything outside their prison directly. Even Incarna are stuck in the spirit world unable to effect the physical one.<br /> <br /> If ennoia started eating physical earth from the inside, gaia would slowly die with the planet and be unable to do anything beyond beg the changing breads for help. Like how the entire fight with the other supernals has been going for millennia, no of them can directly touch each other or earth and they need minions to do it for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are talking about literally killing the Earth to have a chance at devouring Gaia. Since that can't/won't happen, the plan if flawed. And hell, Rorg's physical form was destroyed and he's still kicking around. So while a Celestine might die (this had yet to be proven) from their physical form being destroyed, the Incarna can obviously survive.<br /> And the last statement seems wrong. Their minions battle on earth (and everywhere else) because they battle everywhere. The cause and effect stated above is off (imo).<br /> <br /> I think you put too much stock in the power levels of the Antediluvians. I just do not agree that [Gangrel] is capable of that. Mind you, if for your game Gaia is &quot;merely&quot; an Incarna, then maybe this plan has a chance (and that is still a maybe). Otherwise this has about as much chance as Cappadocius' plan to eat G-d (none).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T03:38:39-07:00","id":967252,"title":"","content":"Probably less, considering the relative power scales involved. Now, I think it would be a fine idea if one of the changes in 5th was that Ennoia managed to transcend the vampire condition by becoming a powerful Gaian spirit and offered her 'descendants' the chance to be transformed from vampires to the members of a new Changing Breed(s). Gangrel who followed Humanity would become human born members while Gangrel who followed the Paths would become animal born members. <br /> <br /> Any who refused to change would remain part of three bloodlines (Country, City, or Mariner). They would have a unique opportunity to become a member of the Changing Breeds whenever they desired, but they would sacrifice their Disciplines to literally start from scratch. Just to be fun, I would say that any ghouls associated with them would be 'forgiven' their age debt and would be permanently transformed into Kinfolk, though they could always become ghouls to other vampires.<br /> <br /> I think that the transformation of Clan Gangrel into a group of Changing Breeds who be a major change to the setting that could explain avoiding Gehenna. Ennoia would probably have a good idea of where her siblings were located, and they could be dragged off into the Umbra and imprisoned by Gaian spirits in a special Realm designed to cater to the dreams of each of the Antediluvians. On occasion, a Mage would stumble upon the Realm and enter a nightmare world based on the dreams of the central Antediluvian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:40:09-07:00","id":967300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=967169#post967169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are talking about literally killing the Earth to have a chance at devouring Gaia. Since that can't/won't happen, the plan if flawed. And hell, Rorg's physical form was destroyed and he's still kicking around. So while a Celestine might die (this had yet to be proven) from their physical form being destroyed, the Incarna can obviously survive.<br /> And the last statement seems wrong. Their minions battle on earth (and everywhere else) because they battle everywhere. The cause and effect stated above is off (imo).<br /> <br /> I think you put too much stock in the power levels of the Antediluvians. I just do not agree that [Gangrel] is capable of that. Mind you, if for your game Gaia is &quot;merely&quot; an Incarna, then maybe this plan has a chance (and that is still a maybe). Otherwise this has about as much chance as Cappadocius' plan to eat G-d (none).</div> </div> </div> </div>Again I really don't see how making gaia an incarnae, celestine, or supernal changes things. At that level spirits cannot effect the physical world directly(though incarnae can if they're summoned or if the thing they represent becomes prominent enough in an area where the guantlet is weak).<br /> <br /> It's not that the ante in question is anywhere near the power level of even a weak incarnae. Same how a human can't really do much if they contract a parasite, you have to go to a doctor and have them treat it with medicine as best they can. The human might be many time bigger and stronger than the tiny parasite, but the moment it's where it wants to be you can't do anything without help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:05:02-07:00","id":967638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=967056#post967056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um, why couldn't a it? If you were to set off enough nukes and destroy the moon, luna would die and wouldn't be able to do sh*t about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicitly untrue in Werewolf's cosmology; Celestines are greater than the material thing the represent and can survive its destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:16:21-07:00","id":967643,"title":"","content":"And Gaia is greater than a Celestine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:17:40-07:00","id":967646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=967643#post967643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Gaia is greater than a Celestine.</div> </div> </div> </div>And furthermore, even dissenting voices about her centrality place her as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:20:48-07:00","id":967648,"title":"","content":"Hypothetically, Gaia could survive the destruction of the Earth and, with Her powers, reform the Earth in a more pleasing form from the resulting debris (whether She would remake Humans would be anyone's guess).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T00:00:01-07:00","id":967800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=967648#post967648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hypothetically, Gaia could survive the destruction of the Earth and, with Her powers, reform the Earth in a more pleasing form from the resulting debris (whether She would remake Humans would be anyone's guess).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man. I am now imagining the expression on the faces of the Garou when, in a hypothetical Apocalypse plot, it is revealed that the whole death and destruction cased by Wyrm and Garou alike is a plot by Gaia to cause exactly that. Psyke!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-12-2016, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T05:52:53-07:00","id":967876,"title":"","content":"yeah, that would be quite fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T06:44:32-07:00","id":967897,"title":"","content":"The real question would be could the Garou somehow convince Gaia to reuse rather than to recycle? <br /> <br /> On another note, how do you think that it would effect things if the Gangrel were given the option to be transformed from members of the vampire clans to members of the changing breeds because their Antediluvian was forgiven by Gaia and transformed into a powerful Incarna? I think that revelation would make their exodus from the Camarilla sensible, as they would have been unconsciously cutting ties to vampire society in preparation for their transformation, with the few within the Anarchs, Camarilla, and Sabbat being the ones who will refuse the transformation. If their current ghouls were also forgiven their 'age debt' and transformed into Kinfolk, I could imagine that, given the connection of the Gangrel to their animalistic Beast, most of the Gangrel who decided to transform would not regret their choice.<br /> <br /> Of course, the changing breeds might be confused by the sudden influx of around 4,000 new members (and tens of thousands of new Kinfolk), but I think that they would eventually accept their new members because they were created by Gaia's mercy (though the Garou would likely look down upon their new Tribe). I would think that the Gangrel would transform into animals that corresponded to their attack forms, so many American Gangrel would become Garou, effectively starting a new Tribe. Bears, lynxes, and hyenas are mentioned as alternative fight forms in the Lore of the Clans, so they would also find themselves joining the Gurahl, Bastet, and Ajaba as new members, and those changing breeds could use the additions. Even if 2,000 became Garou, that would make them the second largest tribe of Garou after the Black Spiral Dancers. Even if the rest were divided among the other predatory Changing Breeds (Ajaba, Bastet, Gurahl, Mokole, Rokea, etc), that would offer large population increases for some of the rarest creatures on the Earth. Just something to think about...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:39:01-07:00","id":967986,"title":"","content":"I think that it might be interesting for Gangrel to become a kind of Gaian creature that is no long a vampire, I can't see them becoming Garou though. They just seem too different on a fundamental spiritual level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:46:31-07:00","id":967991,"title":"","content":"Are they automatically purified of all Wyrm taint or do they still carry an aura of their former existence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:26:03-07:00","id":968140,"title":"","content":"I think that if the vampires are forgiven, they would be purified of all Wyrm taint. As for the vampires being fundamentally different than the Garou, they are, but they would have to gain a Gaian soul to replace their missing human Avatar or else they would just die, so they would either have to become one of the Changing Breeds or one of the Kami. They would be culturally different than the other Changing Breeds though because they have personally benefited from the grace of Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T21:33:57-07:00","id":968359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965930-vampires-and-gaia?p=968140#post968140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that if the vampires are forgiven, they would be purified of all Wyrm taint. As for the vampires being fundamentally different than the Garou, they are, but they would have to gain a Gaian soul to replace their missing human Avatar or else they would just die, so they would either have to become one of the Changing Breeds or one of the Kami. They would be culturally different than the other Changing Breeds though because they have personally benefited from the grace of Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally find it more interesting if they became their own weird type of Changing Breed, and still carried a certain amount of Wyrm taint. It creates a situation where the other Gaians have to learn to deal with their weird new relatives and adapt as they find their niche in the cosmic ecosystem. <br /> <br /> As an aside, its a little off-putting to continue using the term &quot;forgiven&quot; considering most vampires aren't vampires by choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T21:42:33-07:00","id":968361,"title":"","content":"If they are Wyrm-tainted, they will just be destroyed by the rest of the Changing Breeds and go extinct because, unlike the Black Spiral Dancers, they will not have any Wyrm allies to help them against the Bastet, Garou, Mokole, etc. Anyway, why would Gaia leave a job half done? No, if you want it to end up with anything other than the Gangrel become lunch, they have to be purified by Gaia.<br /> <br /> While vampires do not choose to become vampires, they choose their actions afterwards. A vampire can decide to just drink animal blood, with one dose of human blood per month, but the majority of them do not. They choose to prey on humans to the exclusion of animals. Gangrel especially do not have an excuse, since they are supposed to be closer to animals than any other vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T22:27:03-07:00","id":968374,"title":"","content":"I've generally preferred to use Spiritus as a discipline that can be learned only by Vampires who have through proof of virtue, services rendered, and soul-searing purification and associated metaphysical concessions (including the loss of the capacity to sire childer or produce ghouls, and often accompanied by gain of merits/flaws like Inoffensive to Animals, Lunacy, Vulnerability to Silver, Aura of Normalcy, etc.) been permanently attuned to Gaia and so can invoke the energies of Spirits for aid (with level 4 changed to a weaker, voluntary boon from present Gaian spirits- Spiritus 5 is basically Vampire-Crinos anyway). Vampires who slave their souls to the Wyrm also get an analogous malefic version of Spiritus. There's no such thing as Ahrimanes, and Spiritus itself can never be taught to other Vampires or developed innately (although Abominations might also possess it to represent their residual affinity for the spirit world- level 5 for an Abomination is probably replaced with a Stepping Sideways type effect- something they in my version would otherwise lose upon the Embrace and associated evisceration of their connections to the Umbra and the gifts of Gaia). A few severely tainted bloodlines can never undergo the Gaian version of this process- Baali, Lhiannan (who already have an interfering anchor to a particular, malevolent spirit), Lasombra Abyss Mystics and likely those with any substantive investment in Obtenebration, etc., even if in some enormously unlikely event one of their get might break from his ancestry and make strenuous contributions in that vein (and somehow manage to induce Lupines etc. he encountered in doing so to not murder him on sight).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 09-13-2016, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T09:52:10-07:00","id":968579,"title":"","content":"Well, Gaia doesn't seem to turn normal humans into werewolves, even kinfolk need a Wyrmy ritual and some dead Garou. So it seems unlikely then that Gaia would turn Wyrmy vampires into Garou. It seems more likely, if Gaia were going to cure vampires, that she would turn them human again or destroy them and allow them to return to the natural cycle.<br /> <br /> Though, that is the boring option right? We want something more interesting than that. Vampires are powerful supernatural beings, maybe Gaia can utilize some of that power for herself. So she could turn them into something completely new, creatures which utilize some of the vampiric power but are now creatures of Gaia instead of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> What would this creature be like? Well, let's use a vampire as a template and try to remove the things that conflict with Gaia. Well, one thing, vampires shouldn't be undead. They should be alive. So let's make them physically alive instead of undead. They probably shouldn't be immortal either, as living creatures they could breed and reproduce though. Drinking blood is alright with Gaia, as there are plenty of blood drinking animals, so let's keep the blood drinking and maybe give them the Gift of Apis Bardo power, to make feeding on animals a bit more beneficial. Maybe they would become more resistant to sunlight, but still maintain a bit of a nocturnal nature. They should probably lose the ability to create ghouls and create bond bonds, that seems a bit Wyrmy. They would likely lose their immortality and age, perhaps at a reduced rate. I'm not sure what mechanical changes to make. Maybe replace Humanity with some kind of Gaian purity which, if it gets low enough, can cause them to become regular vampires again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}